1
00:00:04,054 --> 00:00:09,950
Banks generate mountains of transaction data
but deliver it as an unreadable table. Customers disengage.

2
00:00:09,950 --> 00:00:14,050
Banker's Wrapped turns that data into a
personalized, narrated recap video —

3
00:00:14,050 --> 00:00:19,687
Genblaze is the sole AI layer, Backblaze B2
the source of truth for every session.

4
00:00:23,066 --> 00:00:26,262
Here's the raw material —
just rows, dates, and numbers.

5
00:00:32,052 --> 00:00:34,552
See it live, right now —
no mockup, no slides.

6
00:00:39,034 --> 00:00:43,250
Connect a bank in one click through Plaid,
or just upload a CSV.

7
00:00:43,250 --> 00:00:46,190
Same pipeline either way —
zero friction, zero forking.

8
00:01:00,070 --> 00:01:05,770
Four typed agents take it from there — parsing,
analytics, a narrative script, and scene generation —

9
00:01:05,770 --> 00:01:10,770
all routed through the Genblaze SDK. GMI Cloud
Seedream paints five scenes in parallel,

10
00:01:10,770 --> 00:01:16,531
OpenAI TTS narrates them, and FFmpeg composes
the final video, live, in under two minutes.

11
00:01:36,200 --> 00:01:40,700
Meet the Financial Builder — your personality,
your story, playing right now.

12
00:01:47,054 --> 00:01:53,750
Every artifact lands on Backblaze B2 — fourteen files,
ten types, from the input CSV to the final video —

13
00:01:53,750 --> 00:01:58,625
each one hashed and verifiable, with full
generation provenance you can inspect yourself.

14
00:02:13,300 --> 00:02:17,500
Refresh the page after a full backend redeploy —
the recap still plays.

15
00:02:17,500 --> 00:02:19,400
B2 is the source of truth.

16
00:02:22,925 --> 00:02:27,000
Ninety-nine percent test coverage,
a hard CI gate, structured logging,

17
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:31,079
and twelve architecture decision records —
this isn't a prototype.

18
00:02:38,666 --> 00:02:41,650
One connection. Five scenes.
Your financial story —

19
00:02:41,650 --> 00:02:44,626
Banker's Wrapped, built on
Genblaze and Backblaze B2.
